y, semantic labels and causal relationships need formalisation and independent evaluation. The six passing tests should not be treated as evidence of natural-language reasoning performance.\n\nThe next milestone I would prioritise is not an 85-million-parameter training run. It is a small, rigorous benchmark demonstrating that the kernel can take previously unseen propositions, infer their relevant relationships, transform them according to your four rules, and compare two IS complexes correctly using evidence rather than manually assigned coordinates.\n\nIf it succeeds there, your 13,000 stories give you a path to scale it. If it fails, the benchmark will show exactly which part of the geometry or semantics needs changing.\n\nThat is why I think the project is worth pursuing: the central representation is specific enough to implement and test, and it gives you a concrete way to investigate whether your AEC framework can improve machine reasoning. The architecture has not proved that outcome yet, but there is a plausible experimental route to finding out.\n\nCertainty: 94% on the assessment of the supplied prototype; confidence in the proposed architecture's eventual performance remains undetermined.","idx":10,"updated":"2026-10-16T07:58:39.412478+00:00","source":"chatgpt","topic_id":86395,"topic_name":"semantic / mechanism / theory reality","score":0.655,"matching_chunks":15},{"chat_id":"gemini-98cfc6bf63e2a8f4","title":"Google Gemini","text":"\nPasso 6 — rodar cd backend && ..\\.tools\\apache-maven-3.9.15\\bin\\mvn.cmd test (ou wrapper disponível). Testes relevantes: PersonalityCategoryTest (falha se category faltar ou for inválida), ReligionFilterTest (falha se religions faltar, tiver valor inválido ou estiver vazio com religiao ≤ 35), PersonalityCategoryMatchTest, IdeologyPersonalityMappingTest, ProfileMatchScorerTest, ScorerBenchmarkTest, QuizFlowAutomationTest, SharedResultsTest. Corrigir causa raiz de qualquer falha, nunca pular.\n\n\nPasso 7 — rodar python profile-audit/compatibility.py personality {id} para calcular as duas personalidades, duas ideologias e dois países mais compatíveis com o vetor recém-criado (mesmo algoritmo de ProfileMatchScorer.java). Nunca estimar esses matches de cabeça.\nAs perguntas de arquétipo fazem parte da auditoria do Passo 5: o prompt termina com o bloco de python profile-audit/profile_vector.py --prompt-block, a saída traz o bloco archetype e o vetor soma as alternativas escolhidas, como no quiz do usuário (ver \"Perguntas de arquétipo\" em profile-audit/README.md). Liste as escolhas no resumo do Passo 8.\n\n\nPasso 8 — apresentar resumo ao usuário: catálogo/id/name, resumo do vetor, religions escolhido (com a razão), livro adicionado a books.json (ou por que nenhum), os matches calculados no passo 7 com percentual exato, confirmação de testes, lista de arquivos tocados.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRegras que não podem ser quebradas\n\n","idx":59,"updated":"2026-10-18T14:35:04.990826+00:00","source":"gemini","topic_id":86435,"topic_name":"modelo / perfis / perfil","score":0.655,"matching_chunks":93},{"chat_id":"gemini-7b63c5493c112114","title":"Formalizing Memory-Induced Implicit Scrupulosity - Google Gemini","text":"I will now update the clinical formulation to integrate this critical phenomenological distinction: the fear is not merely instant panic over a word choice, but rather the **temporal erosion of inferential provenance**—the dread that forgetting *how* you derived an insight or conclusion leaves you defenseless, unable to explain yourself, and increasingly distrustful of your own past reasoning.\n\n[[CANVAS: Memory-Induced Implicit Scrupulosity Formulation]]\n\nI have restructured the formulation to center on **the temporal decay of reasoning provenance and the dread of defenselessness**.\n\nDoes the updated framework capture how the doubt evolves as time passes, or would you like to explore targeted strategies for tolerating the urge to mentally \"re-prove\" your conclusions?\n\n[user] You